WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.341
"The parade starts in five minutes!" yelled Katie.

2
00:00:07.342 --> 00:00:10.019
"The wagons are ready!" called Joy.

3
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.524
The twins ran to the front of the parade.

4
00:00:13.525 --> 00:00:18.214
Mr. and Mrs. Pinker sat up high in a covered wagon.

5
00:00:18.215 --> 00:00:21.957
The Pinker children crowded behind them.

6
00:00:21.958 --> 00:00:27.893
"They’re traveling just like Howard Lightfoot Jackson and his family!" cried Joy.

7
00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.607
"Who?" asked Katie.

8
00:00:30.608 --> 00:00:34.791
"The first family in Willow Creek!" answered Joy.

9
00:00:34.792 --> 00:00:37.718
"Huh?" Katie stared at her twin.

10
00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:40.168
"What do you mean?"

11
00:00:40.169 --> 00:00:46.675
Before Joy could answer, Mr. Pinker shook the reins and his horses started moving.

12
00:00:46.676 --> 00:00:48.992
AJ came running.

13
00:00:48.993 --> 00:00:52.964
"Katie! Ms. Henderson is here!" he yelled.

14
00:00:52.965 --> 00:00:55.952
"She’s in the Model T!"

15
00:00:55.953 --> 00:00:58.545
"Who?" asked Joy.

16
00:00:58.546 --> 00:01:03.376
"The oldest person in Willow Creek!" said AJ.

17
00:01:03.377 --> 00:01:08.365
"What?" cried Joy.

18
00:01:08.366 --> 00:01:15.338
"Hello, kids!" Ms. Henderson called. "I’ve come to the parade!"

19
00:01:15.339 --> 00:01:17.779
"Let’s get this car started,"

20
00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.737
said Grandpa Henderson, rubbing his hands together.

21
00:01:21.738 --> 00:01:25.845
"First, we pull this and turn that."

22
00:01:25.846 --> 00:01:31.461
Grandpa Henderson jumped out of the car and hurried around to the front.

23
00:01:31.462 --> 00:01:35.170
"Now I turn and pull this handle."

24
00:01:35.171 --> 00:01:38.902
He turned and pulled.

25
00:01:38.903 --> 00:01:43.130
"It started!" everyone shouted.

26
00:01:43.131 --> 00:01:47.823
"It just takes practice," said Grandpa Henderson.

27
00:01:47.824 --> 00:01:51.938
"It’s running away!" everyone screamed.

28
00:01:51.939 --> 00:01:55.739
The Model T began rolling toward the street.

29
00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.650
"Get in!" cried Ms. Henderson.

30
00:01:59.651 --> 00:02:04.391
Grandpa Henderson jumped in the car beside his sister.

31
00:02:04.392 --> 00:02:08.328
"Here we go!" he shouted.

32
00:02:08.329 --> 00:02:12.946
"See you at the park!" called the Earthworms.

33
00:02:12.947 --> 00:02:18.637
The high school marching band lined up behind a giant birthday cake.

34
00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:22.438
Then Mrs. Penkov blew her whistle.

35
00:02:22.439 --> 00:02:24.672
"Campers!" she called.

36
00:02:24.673 --> 00:02:27.604
"Get into place behind the band!"

37
00:02:27.605 --> 00:02:31.490
Emily and Carlos unrolled the banner.

38
00:02:31.491 --> 00:02:37.363
"The Willow Creek Day Campers!" read Katie. "That’s us!"

39
00:02:37.364 --> 00:02:41.785
The band started playing.

40
00:02:41.786 --> 00:02:44.467
Luke climbed onto his stilts.

41
00:02:44.468 --> 00:02:47.545
"Woo-hoo!" he yelled.

42
00:02:47.546 --> 00:02:51.941
The day campers headed toward Main Street.

43
00:02:51.942 --> 00:02:55.954
As they turned the corner, Joy saw her family.

44
00:02:55.955 --> 00:03:01.545
"Mom, Dad!" she shouted, waving her ribbon twirler.

45
00:03:01.546 --> 00:03:06.530
"Grandpa!" Aunt Sally stood outside Fried Pie

46
00:03:06.531 --> 00:03:11.409
Heaven. "Hello, Aunt Sally!" shouted Katie and

47
00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:16.589
Joy. They turned onto Walnut Street and paraded into the town

48
00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:22.251
park. The band kept playing while everyone ate watermelon and drank

49
00:03:22.252 --> 00:03:28.588
lemonade. Then the mayor made a speech, and the Willow Creek Singers performed old

50
00:03:28.589 --> 00:03:35.601
songs. Finally Mrs. Penkov stepped onto the platform to address the

51
00:03:35.602 --> 00:03:40.488
crowd. "As you know, the day campers had a scavenger hunt this

52
00:03:40.489 --> 00:03:43.726
summer." "Yes, they did. And they were real

53
00:03:43.727 --> 00:03:46.536
pests!" Pete from the post office shouted,

54
00:03:46.537 --> 00:03:49.944
laughing. The crowd laughed

55
00:03:49.945 --> 00:03:52.017
too. Mrs. Penkov

56
00:03:52.018 --> 00:03:54.671
continued. "Now it’s time to announce the

57
00:03:54.672 --> 00:04:02.146
winners. Guess what?" The campers held their

58
00:04:02.147 --> 00:04:04.250
breath. "We have a

59
00:04:04.251 --> 00:04:06.907
tie!" The campers

60
00:04:06.908 --> 00:04:09.186
gasped. "Two teams completed their

61
00:04:09.187 --> 00:04:12.358
lists. Both found Willow Creek

62
00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:21.519
treasures. One team found a piece of history—the oldest grave in Willow Creek at the burial place of the first settling

63
00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.622
family." Mrs. Penkov unrolled a crayon

64
00:04:24.623 --> 00:04:28.762
rubbing. "Howard Lightfoot

65
00:04:28.763 --> 00:04:36.219
Jackson,1848." "The other team found a living treasure—our oldest citizen," continued Mrs. Penkov.

66
00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:41.022
"Cora Mae Henderson—103 years old.

67
00:04:41.023 --> 00:04:45.728
"So the winners are the Tornadoes and the Earthworms!

68
00:04:45.729 --> 00:04:53.396
Each team member wins a ticket for a free day at Big Surf Water Park!" said Mrs. Penkov.

69
00:04:53.397 --> 00:04:58.520
"Big Surf!" cried the Tornadoes and the Earthworms.

70
00:04:58.521 --> 00:05:02.794
"The Double Dip!" cried Joy and Laura.

71
00:05:02.795 --> 00:05:07.404
"The Slippery Spin!" cried Katie and Luke.

72
00:05:07.405 --> 00:05:13.037
The Tornadoes and the Earthworms jumped with joy.

73
00:05:13.038 --> 00:05:20.233
Later that evening, they sat beside the creek and watched fireworks explode in the sky.

74
00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:24.595
"Day camp is over," said Joy with a sigh.

75
00:05:24.596 --> 00:05:30.500
"But we have Willow Creek T-shirts to keep forever," said Laura.

76
00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:34.845
"And we all won the scavenger hunt!" said Luke.

77
00:05:34.846 --> 00:05:39.850
"And we all get to go to Big Surf!" said AJ.

78
00:05:39.851 --> 00:05:50.729
Katie grinned. "Best of all, we still have the rest of the summer to have fun in our Willow Creek!"

